# Go: compiled test binaries + coverage profiles (binaries are built
# in-container; nothing Go-native is ever committed)
*.test
*.out
# Stray `go build ./cmd/guide` output from the server module root
server/guide
# JS installs & build output
node_modules/
dist/
# Env files stay out of git — committed non-secret templates (if any arise)
# get an explicit `!path` negation here, fastapi-family style. The client
# build-env template is public-by-design (Umami placeholders, empty = off).
.env*
!client/.env.example
# Test coverage OUTPUT (Go profiles + Vitest HTML reports). Anchored to
# the repo root: server/tools/coverage/ is the committed coverage GATE
# (check.sh + THRESHOLD.md) and must stay tracked.
/coverage/
# Topic 26 (files-media): the file store's runtime home — uploaded bytes and
# metadata sidecars are runtime data, never source (server/data/).
server/data/
*.log
# OS
.DS_Store
# IDE dirs
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
# In-container flock targets for verification runs (runtime artifacts)
.verify.lock
# Playwright e2e artifacts (host-run suite in e2e/ — reports + browser cache)
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
e2e/.playwright/
.zcode/
